---

<Base title="SEO Audit Reading | Full Site Analysis" description="Comprehensive SEO audit for Reading businesses. Technical health, content gaps, backlink analysis, local SEO review. Actionable recommendations." schema={schema}>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <div class="prose">

      <h1>SEO Audit for Reading Businesses</h1>

      <p>SEO Reading conducts comprehensive SEO audits that provide Reading businesses with a clear picture of their search visibility, technical health, and competitive position. An audit serves as the essential starting point for any effective SEO campaign, as it identifies precisely what is functioning well, what is compromised, and where the highest-impact opportunities reside.</p>

      <div class="quick-answer">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> An SEO audit is a systematic review of your website's technical health, content, backlinks, and local search presence. For Reading businesses, it reveals why you rank where you do and what specific changes will enhance your Google visibility. You receive a prioritised action plan accompanied by a one-hour walkthrough call.
      </div>

      <p>In our experience, most Reading businesses we audit present 20-50 actionable issues that are directly suppressing their rankings. Some constitute quick fixes that yield results within weeks. Others represent strategic gaps requiring planned content or link building. The audit distinguishes between the two and provides a clear sequence to follow.</p>

      <h2>What's Included in an SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>Our audit encompasses five pillars that together determine your search visibility in <strong>Reading</strong> and <strong>Berkshire</strong>.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Technical health</strong> — crawlability, indexation, site speed, Core Web Vitals, structured data, HTTPS, mobile usability</li>
        <li><strong>On-page SEO</strong> — title tags, meta descriptions, heading structure, content quality, keyword targeting, internal linking</li>
        <li><strong>Off-page SEO</strong> — backlink profile, referring domain quality, anchor text distribution, toxic link identification</li>
        <li><strong>Local SEO</strong> — Google Business Profile, local citations, NAP consistency, local pack eligibility, review profile</li>
        <li><strong>Competitor analysis</strong> — benchmarking against 3-5 direct competitors within your Reading market</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Each pillar receives a health score, a list of issues ranked by severity, and specific recommendations with anticipated impact.</p>

      <h2>Technical Health Assessment</h2>

      <p>The technical assessment constitutes the most substantial section of the audit. We crawl your entire site using Screaming Frog and cross-reference findings with Google Search Console data.</p>

      <h3>What We Examine</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Crawlability</strong> — are all important pages reachable? Are robots.txt and meta robots correctly configured? Are there crawl errors reported in Search Console?</li>
        <li><strong>Indexation</strong> — which pages are indexed, which are excluded, and for what reason? Are canonical tags correctly implemented? Is there index bloat from duplicate or thin pages?</li>
        <li><strong>Site speed</strong> — Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS) derived from field data and laboratory testing. Page-by-page speed analysis for your highest-traffic URLs.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured data</strong> — is schema markup present? Is it valid? Are schema types that could earn rich results absent? For Reading businesses, LocalBusiness schema is of critical importance.</li>
        <li><strong>HTTPS</strong> — SSL certificate validity, mixed content, redirect implementation from HTTP to HTTPS.</li>
        <li><strong>Mobile usability</strong> — responsive design issues, touch target sizes, viewport configuration, mobile-specific speed.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>For a more detailed examination of what technical SEO involves and its significance, see our <a href="/technical-seo-reading/">technical SEO services page</a>.</p>

      <h2>Content and Keyword Gap Analysis</h2>

      <p>Your content determines which queries you can rank for. The content audit identifies missed opportunities within the Reading market that your competitors are capturing and you are not.</p>

      <h3>What We Analyse</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Current keyword rankings</strong> — every query for which your site appears in Google, with position, impressions, clicks, and CTR</li>
        <li><strong>Keyword gaps</strong> — queries your competitors rank for that you do not, filtered to Reading-relevant terms</li>
        <li><strong>Content quality</strong> — thin pages, duplicate content, outdated information, pages that target the same keyword (cannibalisation)</li>
        <li><strong>Search intent alignment</strong> — are your pages consistent with what Google seeks to display for each query?</li>
        <li><strong>Striking distance keywords</strong> — queries where you rank in positions 4-20 and a content improvement could advance you into the top 3</li>
      </ul>

      <p>The output is a prioritised list of content opportunities with estimated search volume and recommended page formats. In our experience, many Reading businesses discover that a modest number of content improvements can double their organic traffic within 3-6 months.</p>

      <h2>Backlink Profile Review</h2>

      <p>Backlinks remain among Google's strongest ranking signals. The backlink review examines both the quality and quantity of sites linking to yours.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Referring domain count and quality</strong> — how many unique sites link to you, and what is their authority?</li>
        <li><strong>Anchor text distribution</strong> — is the anchor text natural, or does it suggest manipulative link building?</li>
        <li><strong>Toxic links</strong> — are there spammy or harmful links that could trigger a Google penalty?</li>
        <li><strong>Link velocity</strong> — are you gaining or losing links over time?</li>
        <li><strong>Competitor comparison</strong> — how does your backlink profile compare to Reading competitors within your industry?</li>
      </ul>

      <p>For most Reading businesses, the backlink review reveals that competitors have secured more links from local directories, industry bodies, and Berkshire-based publications. We identify the specific link sources you ought to target.</p>

      <h2>Local SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>Local SEO determines whether your business appears in Google's local pack — the map results displayed for location-based queries. For Reading businesses, this frequently represents the highest-converting search real estate.</p>

      <h3>Google Business Profile</h3>

      <p>We review your Google Business Profile for completeness, accuracy, and optimisation. This encompasses your business categories, description, photographs, opening hours, service area, Q&A, and posts. A fully optimised GBP is, in our assessment, the single most influential local ranking factor.</p>

      <h3>Citations and NAP Consistency</h3>

      <p>Your business name, address, and phone number (NAP) must be consistent across every directory, social profile, and mention online. Inconsistencies confuse Google and weaken local rankings. We examine the major UK directories — Yell, Thomson Local, Yelp, Cylex, FreeIndex — and Reading-specific directories for accuracy.</p>

      <h3>Local Pack Eligibility</h3>

      <p>Not every query triggers a local pack. We identify which of your target keywords display local pack results and whether your business is eligible to appear. For <strong>Reading</strong> businesses competing with firms in <strong>Wokingham</strong>, <strong>Bracknell</strong>, and <strong>Newbury</strong>, local pack visibility can prove the decisive factor in securing a customer.</p>

      <h2>Competitor Analysis</h2>

      <p>An audit conducted without competitive context is incomplete. We benchmark your site against 3-5 direct competitors — businesses that rank for the same Reading-area keywords you seek to win.</p>

      <p>The competitor analysis encompasses:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Domain authority and backlink profile comparison</li>
        <li>Content depth and keyword coverage gaps</li>
        <li>Technical health comparison (speed, mobile, structured data)</li>
        <li>Local SEO presence (GBP reviews, local citations, local content)</li>
        <li>SERP feature ownership (featured snippets, People Also Ask, local pack positions)</li>
      </ul>

      <p>This analysis reveals precisely where investment is required to overtake specific competitors. For a Reading accountancy firm, that may mean creating service pages for specific tax topics their competitors rank for. For a Reading restaurant, it may mean cultivating a review profile that matches the local pack leaders.</p>

      <h2>What You Receive</h2>

      <p>The audit deliverable is practical and actionable. You receive three components:</p>

      <h3>1. Comprehensive Audit Report</h3>

      <p>A detailed document covering every finding across all five pillars. Each issue is described with screenshots, a severity rating, and a specific recommendation. The report typically spans 30-60 pages, depending upon site size.</p>

      <h3>2. Prioritised Action Plan</h3>

      <p>A spreadsheet ranking every recommendation by impact and effort. High-impact, low-effort items are positioned at the top. This serves as your roadmap — work through it sequentially for maximum results in minimum time. Issues are categorised as critical, high, medium, or low priority.</p>

      <h3>3. One-Hour Walkthrough Call</h3>

      <p>We walk through the findings with you, address questions, and discuss implementation options. This ensures you understand not merely what to fix, but the rationale behind each issue and what results to anticipate. In our experience, many Reading business owners find this to be the most valuable component of the audit, as it translates technical findings into commercial terms.</p>

      <h2>Who Needs an SEO Audit</h2>

      <p>An SEO audit is pertinent at several stages of a Reading business's online journey.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>New businesses</strong> near <strong>The Oracle</strong> or <strong>Broad Street</strong> launching their first website require a baseline from which to build</li>
        <li><strong>Established firms</strong> at <strong>Forbury Square</strong> or <strong>Kings Road</strong> whose rankings have plateaued or declined</li>
        <li><strong>Post-redesign</strong> — any business that has recently altered their website design, CMS, or URL structure</li>
        <li><strong>Post-penalty</strong> — businesses that have experienced a sudden, significant ranking decline</li>
        <li><strong>Pre-investment</strong> — before committing to an SEO retainer, an audit clarifies precisely what you are investing in</li>
        <li><strong>Competitive pressure</strong> — when a competitor begins outranking you for your core Reading-area keywords</li>
      </ul>

      <p>If you have never commissioned an SEO audit, there are almost certainly quick wins awaiting discovery on your site. The audit identifies them.</p>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">What is the typical duration of an SEO audit?</h3>
        <p>A comprehensive SEO audit for a standard Reading business website requires 7-14 working days. This encompasses the crawl, data analysis, report preparation, and formulation of your prioritised action plan. Larger sites comprising thousands of pages may necessitate additional time. You will receive a confirmed delivery date upon booking.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">What information must I provide for the audit?</h3>
        <p>We require Google Search Console access (or to be added as a user), Google Analytics access where available, and your principal business objectives. Should you have specific keywords you are targeting or competitors you wish to benchmark against, we welcome those as well. We manage everything else.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">What is the cost of an SEO audit?</h3>
        <p>Our comprehensive SEO audit is offered as a fixed-fee service. The precise cost depends upon site size and complexity. Visit our <a href="/seo-pricing-reading/">pricing page</a> for indicative rates, or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> for a quotation tailored to your site.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">Will you implement the recommendations or solely report them?</h3>
        <p>The audit deliverable comprises a report with prioritised recommendations. Implementation is available as a separate engagement or as part of an ongoing SEO retainer. Many Reading businesses elect to begin with the audit and subsequently transition into monthly SEO management for implementation and monitoring.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">At what intervals should an SEO audit be conducted?</h3>
        <p>A full audit conducted every 12 months represents a sound baseline. If you have recently redesigned your site, migrated platforms, or experienced a significant ranking decline, an immediate audit is warranted. Between full audits, ongoing monitoring identifies issues as they arise.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-question">Do you audit competitor websites as part of the process?</h3>
        <p>Indeed. We benchmark your site against 3-5 direct competitors within the Reading market. This analysis reveals gaps in content, backlinks, and technical implementation that you may exploit. We identify precisely what your competitors execute more effectively and where you already possess an advantage.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-box">
        <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Commission Your SEO Audit</h2>
        <p>Obtain a clear picture of your website's search performance together with a prioritised action plan to improve it. Every audit includes a one-hour walkthrough call.</p>
        <a href="/contact/">Book a Consultation</a>
      </div>

      <p>Prefer a preliminary health check first? Our <a href="/free-seo-audit-reading/">free SEO audit</a> provides a baseline assessment with no obligation. Consult our <a href="/seo-pricing-reading/">pricing page</a> for service costs, or explore our <a href="/technical-seo-reading/">technical SEO</a> offering specifically.</p>

      <p>Back to <a href="/services/">all services</a> or return to <a href="/">SEO Reading homepage</a>.</p>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
